The article in this directory is not ours.

"AES-GCM and breaking it on nonce reuse" was written by frereit (Frederik
Reiter) and published at https://frereit.de/aes_gcm/ under the Creative
Commons Attribution ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0),
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/. The original page carries
that licence in its own footer.

public/original.html is that page as mirrored, byte for byte, together with
the styles, scripts, wasm module and images it loads.

public/index.html is the same page with nema added: one manifest, one script
tag, five inline question anchors, one activities block and an attribution
paragraph at the top and the bottom. Nothing of the article's text, markup or
widgets was changed. public/compare.html shows the exact diff.

This copy, and the nema additions inside it, are published under the same
licence, CC BY-SA 4.0, as the licence requires of a derivative work.
Attribution: frereit, https://frereit.de/aes_gcm/.

The point of the mirror is to show what a learning protocol adds to an
article that already exists, on a real article rather than a demo one. If
frereit would rather we did not host this copy, we will take it down: write
to the address on https://nema.migarci2.dev.

The rest of the nema repository is under the licence in the repository root
LICENSE file. This file governs apps/aesgcm/public only.
